1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:06,106
How much stronger is acetic acid than hydrocyanic acid, at the same concentration?

2
00:00:06,106 --> 00:00:14,466
Strength goes as the degree of ionisation, which, as we will see, is the square root of K a over C.

3
00:00:14,466 --> 00:00:19,205
So the ratio is the square root of the ratio of the K a values.

